11
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:24,500
All right, well, good morning, everyone.

12
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:27,400
Thank you all for joining us this morning.

13
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,300
My name is Ryan.

14
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:31,000
If we haven't met yet, I have the privilege of being one of the pastors here.

15
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,880
And as you can tell, we are continuing our series on the parables.

16
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:37,640
This is week three of the parables of Jesus.

17
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:46,800
And I just want to remind you that one of our core values as a church is that we rely on the written and living word of God.

18
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:49,480
So we are a people of the Scriptures.

19
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:56,060
We are a people of the Scriptures who believe that the Scriptures were given to us to reveal Jesus to us.

20
00:01:56,060 --> 00:02:00,660
That John says he, in the beginning was the word, and the word became flesh and dwelt among us.

21
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:04,420
That all of the Scriptures are intended to point us to Jesus.

22
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:09,540
And so when Jesus talks, we want to pay close attention to it.

23
00:02:09,540 --> 00:02:15,320
And parables are a significant part of Jesus' teaching, of Jesus' talking.

24
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:22,480
Depending on how you categorize the parables, people think there are 30 to 40 parables in the Gospels.

25
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:28,840
And one-third, one-third of the red letters that you will find in the Gospels are parables.

26
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:35,860
Now, because of that fact, we cannot cover them all because it would be a two-year-long series.

27
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:38,900
And we all know that you guys' attention span is not that good.

28
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:41,380
Nor is mine.

29
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:44,720
So I will put the judgment on myself there.

30
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:48,260
But my goal is to cover a few different types of parables

31
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:52,280
and kind of help you understand how I am doing my best,

32
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:55,000
how we as communicators on the stage are interpreting the parables

33
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,020
so that you have the tools to read the parables for yourself,

34
00:02:58,020 --> 00:03:00,720
to interpret them for yourself.

35
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:05,220
And Kent opened up the series by saying that parables are indirect communication

36
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:08,420
aimed at challenging previously held assumptions.

37
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:15,080
They're a way in which Jesus is able to get through the back window of our imagination, of our hearts.

38
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:16,420
They appeal to our imagination.

39
00:03:17,540 --> 00:03:23,500
Most of us, by the time we get to a certain age, have concrete ideas about what we believe.

40
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:26,180
And the same was true for Jesus' audience.

41
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:30,000
They had concrete ideas specifically about what they believed the kingdom of heaven

42
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,460
and the kingdom of God was like.

43
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:34,820
And Jesus came saying the kingdom of heaven is something totally different

44
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:36,740
than what you are thinking it is like.

45
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:38,760
And they struggled with that.

46
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:42,380
And so he told these stories to try and help engage their imagination

47
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:44,940
so that they didn't just shut down from what he was saying,

48
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:49,220
but they were able to walk away from his teaching and marinate on it and think about it.

49
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:55,860
In context, when we read the parables, we first need to understand what Jesus is saying to his original audience.

50
00:03:55,860 --> 00:04:01,900
The church has a habit of reading the parables as if they were written directly to us,

51
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:06,980
as if Jesus is speaking past his audience to a future audience.

52
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:08,660
And the reality is that's not the case.

53
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:10,960
He was speaking to the group of people that were in front of him.

54
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:13,900
Now, they were recorded for us and have significance for us.

55
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:19,460
But in order for us to understand them properly, we have to understand Jesus' intent first.

56
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:25,020
One scholar I really like says that there's a difference between intention and significance.

57
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:29,920
So the intention is what Jesus was trying to communicate to his audience.

58
00:04:29,920 --> 00:04:34,460
And the significance is then how do we understand what he was intending to say to his audience?

59
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:35,960
How does that apply to us?

60
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:37,840
What does that mean for our lives?

61
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:46,660
As I was prepping for this series, I was trying to find a neat, clean, organized way that scholars agree on characterizing the parables.

62
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:49,280
Still looking?

63
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:49,940
Yeah.

64
00:04:49,940 --> 00:04:55,760
Yeah, I found at least 50 different ways that different scholars categorize the parables.

65
00:04:55,760 --> 00:05:02,220
And so I ended up settling on this one categorization because it's only three categories.

66
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:06,260
And we all know three is better than seven or 11, which some of the other ones had.

67
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:15,500
So the three categories that we're going to work through for the rest of the series are the surprising parables about the surprising arrival of God's kingdom,

68
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:18,380
the surprising ethic of God's kingdom.

69
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:24,140
And then as we get closer to Jerusalem, as the temperature is rising around Jesus and his teaching,

70
00:05:24,140 --> 00:05:27,680
his parables get significantly more pointed and challenging.

71
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:30,560
And those are parables of crisis of choice.

72
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:34,840
He's putting the arrival and the ethic of the kingdom in front of his audience.

73
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:41,240
And he's saying, there's about to come a time where you're going to have to choose which of these kingdoms you're going to live for.

74
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:44,180
So last week and this week is going to be the arrival.

75
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:47,020
We'll move to the ethic next week and we'll end with choice.

76
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:52,280
But I just wanted to give you a framework so you knew that I did have a plan and an intention behind the series.

77
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,720
Sound good?

78
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,200
All right.

79
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:56,280
With all that, yeah, let's go.

80
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:56,900
Rachel's ready.

81
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:57,800
She's like, enough of this.

82
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:58,540
Let's get started.

83
00:05:58,620 --> 00:05:58,740
All right.

84
00:05:58,740 --> 00:06:03,240
With all that recap and context, let's pray and dive into our two parables today.

85
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:09,880
They are the shortest of the parables, relatively easy to understand intellectually, but extremely challenging for our lives.

86
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:10,700
So let's pray.

87
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:13,760
Father in heaven, Abba.

88
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:18,920
We thank you for Jesus.

89
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:31,760
We thank you for the Scriptures that, from Genesis all the way through Revelation, point us to Jesus, the ultimate fulfillment of your purposes and your plan to redeem this broken world.

90
00:06:32,620 --> 00:06:36,880
To bring it back to rights, to reconcile it to its good design.

91
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:42,860
God, right now we experience so much brokenness, so much pain, so much heartache, so much loss, so much difficulty.

92
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:48,600
And we're holding to, clinging tightly to the truth that that is not how you intended it to be.

93
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:55,360
And that Jesus is the linchpin and redeeming and restoring all of it back to your will and your way.

94
00:06:55,360 --> 00:07:02,120
And so as we wait in the blurry middle, in the confusing middle, God, give us faith to see who you are.

95
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:05,040
Faith to see what you're doing behind the scenes.

96
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:11,420
And God, bring your kingdom on earth as it is in heaven.

97
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:13,540
In Jesus' name I pray.

98
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:14,380
Amen.

99
00:07:14,380 --> 00:07:24,240
I have this recurring daydream that usually pops into my head on long car rides when I'm trying to pass the time.

100
